.TH LINTO 1 "October 2026" "linto" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linto \- dispatch command-line tools from the Linux Tools collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linto
.RI [ --help ]
.br
.B linto
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B linto help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B linto completion
.RI { bash | zsh | fish }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linto
is a command dispatcher for the local Linux Tools collection. It locates tools
relative to the
.B linto
launcher, so commands can be run from any working directory. A tool receives
the arguments supplied after its command name.
.PP
With no arguments or with
.BR --help ,
.B linto
prints a usage summary and the available executable shell-script commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Print the general tool guide. With a command name, display help for that tool.
For most commands this runs the tool with
.BR --help ;
some commands provide dispatcher-specific help instead.
.TP
.B completion SHELL
Print shell completion setup instructions for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
or
.BR fish .
This prints instructions; it does not modify shell configuration files.
.TP
.I command
Run the named tool. The dispatcher looks first for an executable file named
.I command
beside the launcher, then for an executable
.I command.sh
file. The tool's standard input, output, error, and exit status are passed
through.
.PP
The alias
.B slug
runs
.BR stripaccents .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , --help
Print the usage summary when given as the first argument. To request help for a
specific tool, use
.B "linto COMMAND --help"
or
.BR "linto help COMMAND" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The dispatcher exits with status 0 when it successfully prints its own help or
completion instructions. Invalid dispatcher usage, an unsupported completion
shell, or an unknown command results in status 2. For a dispatched command,
.B linto
returns that command's exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the available commands:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto --help
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run a tool and request its help:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto render --help
.RE
.fi
.PP
Open a file with the Zed tool:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto zed Makefile
.RE
.fi
.PP
Print the Bash completion setup line:
.PP
.nf
.RS
linto completion bash
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I linto
The command dispatcher.
.TP
.I linto-guide
The general guide shown by
.BR "linto help" .
.TP
.I completions/linto.bash
.TQ
.I completions/linto.zsh
.TQ
.I completions/linto.fish
Shell completion definitions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR fish (1)
